#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:62 38c1f8b9b26245b38b7d0f6ca544b493
msgid ""
"Look up detailed information about any biomedical entity in the Monarch "
"Initiative knowledge grap..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst aa22284a1e6d46129507f248f6763c84
msgid "MonarchV3_get_entity tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:68 7b3d7b394d344ff7a90a680863975437
msgid "**Name**: ``MonarchV3_get_entity``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:70 844fb58259a64a998f679ba147c9b4b2
msgid ""
"**Description**: Look up detailed information about any biomedical entity"
" in the Monarch Initiative knowledge graph by its CURIE identifier. "
"Supports genes (HGNC), diseases (MONDO, OMIM), phenotypes (HP), variants,"
" and more. Returns the entity name, category, description, synonyms, "
"cross-references, and species. Example: HGNC:11998 returns TP53 gene with"
" cross-refs to ENSEMBL, OMIM; MONDO:0005148 returns type 2 diabetes "
"mellitus with detailed description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:74 cf67802287df4519be841ceb8d841632
msgid ""
"``entity_id`` (string) (required) Entity CURIE identifier. Examples: "
"'HGNC:11998' (TP53), 'HGNC:1100' (BRCA1), 'MONDO:0005148' (type 2 "
"diabetes), 'HP:0001250' (seizure), 'OMIM:191170' (Li-Fraumeni syndrome)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:91 a21097ec7e5841f0ae3b586051b5ed77
msgid "**MonarchV3_get_histopheno** (Type: MonarchV3Tool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:93 9569dac689174ad3a55e65ae1e819b16
msgid ""
"Get the phenotype profile of a disease grouped by body system from the "
"Monarch Initiative. Return..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst 24201cc160244379bb2aa53f9fc081db
msgid "MonarchV3_get_histopheno tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:99 26db70f4fb9e4eac910e5165b1e3dd71
msgid "**Name**: ``MonarchV3_get_histopheno``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:101 1895f083e459480da53dedbcb4cb338c
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get the phenotype profile of a disease grouped by body "
"system from the Monarch Initiative. Returns counts of phenotypic features"
" (HPO terms) organized by anatomical system (e.g., nervous\\_system, "
"skeletal\\_system, eye, cardiovascular\\_system). Only systems with at "
"least one phenotype are returned, sorted by count descending. Useful for "
"understanding which organ systems are most affected by a disease. "
"Example: MONDO:0007947 (Marfan syndrome) returns high counts for "
"head\\_neck (58), musculature (58), skeletal\\_system (56), eye (31)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:105 99cb1f901e4341cabf0f68b6dc641344
msgid ""
"``entity_id`` (string) (required) Disease CURIE identifier. Examples: "
"'MONDO:0007947' (Marfan syndrome), 'MONDO:0005148' (type 2 diabetes), "
"'MONDO:0004975' (Alzheimer disease), 'MONDO:0005015' (diabetes mellitus)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:122 04149f61f95e47f2b8c369ed0f397a4a
msgid "**MonarchV3_get_mappings** (Type: MonarchV3Tool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:124 5f3cd70aeea744ff8c382cf0f8dbdee9
msgid ""
"Get cross-ontology mappings for a biomedical entity from the Monarch "
"Initiative. Returns equivale..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst 1a485ef7426a4f3d9535a83d2c1f5c5d
msgid "MonarchV3_get_mappings tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:130 faa12fb4f7b444e4ba8befd47b0c295e
msgid "**Name**: ``MonarchV3_get_mappings``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:132 55b5c5cc4e0f40ef9dc6275c551ae33a
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get cross-ontology mappings for a biomedical entity from"
" the Monarch Initiative. Returns equivalence mappings between ontology "
"identifiers, such as MONDO to OMIM, ICD10, SNOMED CT, NCIT, MESH, DOID, "
"and Orphanet. Useful for translating disease identifiers across coding "
"systems (e.g., for clinical data integration, ICD-10 billing codes, or "
"linking to OMIM entries). Example: MONDO:0005148 (type 2 diabetes) maps "
"to ICD10CM:E11, DOID:9352, OMIM:125853, MESH:D003924."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:136 31558e16055e49eb8d1606bd434acf78
msgid ""
"``entity_id`` (string) (required) Entity CURIE identifier to find "
"mappings for. Examples: 'MONDO:0005148' (type 2 diabetes), "
"'MONDO:0007947' (Marfan syndrome), 'HP:0001250' (seizure)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:139 abc98e620f494b8fac7f863ba4e87156
msgid ""
"``limit`` (integer) (optional) Maximum number of mappings to return "
"(default: 20, max: 100)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:156 cd68cf8d7eb447c687e18fa34a98d6b3
msgid "**MonarchV3_phenotype_similarity_search** (Type: MonarchV3Tool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:158 7a903c06d51b47228fe9165c2ecac1b6
msgid ""
"Find diseases that best match a set of phenotypes (HPO terms) using "
"semantic similarity from the ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst 5d984e2201ee4951a6076ed202cedce0
msgid "MonarchV3_phenotype_similarity_search tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:164 8b98d2b8c36642b88bdb8c235cdbae78
msgid "**Name**: ``MonarchV3_phenotype_similarity_search``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:166 58f6031e1bce4dd4944d8043503473c6
msgid ""
"**Description**: Find diseases that best match a set of phenotypes (HPO "
"terms) using semantic similarity from the Monarch Initiative. Given a "
"patient phenotype profile as a list of HPO IDs, returns diseases ranked "
"by phenotype overlap score. Uses information content-based similarity "
"(AncestorInformationContent metric). Essential for rare disease "
"differential diagnosis: input observed phenotypes, get ranked candidate "
"diseases. Example: [HP:0001250 (seizure), HP:0001249 (intellectual "
"disability), HP:0002353 (EEG abnormality)] returns diseases like "
"intellectual disability AR 31, Dravet syndrome ranked by semantic "
"similarity score."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:170 ddabbdf6739e42abbc3e2f8906adf03a
msgid ""
"``phenotypes`` (array) (required) List of HPO term CURIEs representing "
"observed phenotypes. Examples: ['HP:0001250', 'HP:0001249', 'HP:0002353']"
" for seizure + intellectual disability + EEG abnormality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:173 011c1db8dd694866abe8aaf91a19d6dd
msgid ""
"``group`` (string) (optional) Entity group to search against. Default: "
"'Human Diseases'. Options: 'Human Diseases', 'Mouse', 'Rat', 'Zebrafish',"
" 'C. elegans', 'Drosophila'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:176 0eb5e5b275084b2caf2a10d7c533afef
msgid ""
"``limit`` (integer) (optional) Maximum number of matching diseases to "
"return (default: 10, max: 50)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/monarch_v3_tools.rst:193 e51f3b976b88495db6165e7b8b5e7370
